WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.000
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:10.120
I want to thank George who sent me this problem. The problem was given to George by his seventh grade math teacher, Ms. V.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.599
Consider the following table.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:20.938
All numbers in the first column have been increased by the same percentage P to give the results in the second column.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:26.759
The resulting numbers are coded. Each digit is replaced by a letter.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.040
A given letter stands for the same digit every time it appears in that column.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.860
What is the value of P, the percentage increase?

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:45.620
Now I have received an email from a blind person who requested that when possible I read out the numbers that are on the screen.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.700
So let me read out this table. It consists of eight rows with two columns.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:01:00.660
The first column consists of a two-digit number and the second column consists of two letters, so let me read it out row by row

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:03.610
20 G C

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.379
15 I J

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:07.180
45 A C

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.920
35 C G

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.060
70 J C

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.600
80 H F

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.120
25 E B

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.160
and 60 D G

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.700
So can you figure out this seemingly impossible seventh-grade math problem?

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.620
Give it a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:42.620
So there may be many ways to solve this problem; here's how I figured it out and you can share your method in the comments.

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.148
Since the second column has distinct whole numbers,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.839
we can limit the search to positive fractional increases.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.060
So let's search for a common factor of the numbers in the first column.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.920
I consider the numbers thirty-five and twenty.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.989
Thirty-five is equal to five times seven and twenty is equal to five times four so

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.840
We can consider the common factor of five.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:19.240
This gives the possibilities of fractional increases of 1/5, 2/5, 3/5, 4/5, and 5/5.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.040
These correspond to percentage increases of 20%, 40%, 60%, 80%, and 100%

00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:28.069
Which one is it?

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:35.239
Notice that 80 increased by 25% is equal to 100 which is a three-digit number

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.950
But the resulting number for 80 has only two digits

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.540
Therefore the percentage increase 
has to be less than 25%.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:52.620
This means the percentage increase is equal to 20% and you can check that that works.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:03:01.660
For example, 20 increased by 20% is equal to 24, and 35 increased by 20% is equal to 42, and

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.880
And these are the same digits in the answer just reversed.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.530
24, 42 - and G C and C G

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:15.380
And you could check it works. There are no other contradictions in the table so the correct answer is 20%.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.680
Did you figure it out?

